      "role": "user",
      "content": "i dont think i can just walk into HR and ask \"hey why is my chair spying on my heart rate\" lol they'll just think im losing it or mark me as a liability. it's too subtle for that. i've noticed it's specifically heavy in the lumbar support area and i can swear i feel a slight vibration when i'm actually concentrating hard. if i want to just stay under the radar and keep my privacy without making a huge scene, what are some things i can do to keep my vital signs or posture patterns from being read accurately?",
